e that strikes only cancer cells. Palette: near-black metallic gunmetal, faint vanishing violet, pinpoint white sparks, cold halogen grey-blue.\n\nWorld (fixed): a kingdom that never gathers: its whole people are single dark-violet sparks hidden one by one in rock cracks across the continent; only on a glittering plain of black crystal do they gather for a few moments into a citadel of dark metal that begins to boil away in its own heat before it is ever finished, its half-built spires already thinning into faint vapour. Her costume and setting belong to this world.\n\nCostume (choose one of ours, then add your own idea): pick ONE of these costume shapes from our set and keep its overall silhouette — 1) leather armor with a short cloak, a lowered hood, bracers and boots — a light, agile ranger's silhouette; 2) a long floor-length robe with a high collar, wide sleeves and a shoulder mantle — a tall, mysterious mage's silhouette; 3) a light breastplate and bracers with robe panels split from the waist — half armor, half robe; 4) angular, spiked dark plate armor and a long cape with torn edges — a sharp, menacing silhouette; 5) a fur cloak, leather straps, minimal metal plates and bone and tooth ornaments — a rugged, wild warrior silhouette. Then add one signature idea of your own drawn from her element, built into the construction of the outfit itself rather than as a print or a loose accessory — e.g. plates or cloth layered like crystals, scales or flames, a hem or sleeve cut into a shape from her element. Build it in this world's materials and our colours below.\n\nCostume colours (ours): near-black metallic gunmetal, faint vanishing violet, pinpoint white sparks, cold halogen grey-blue.\n\nHair colour (fixed — ours): jet-black metallic hair with a faint violet sheen, scattered with a few tiny white pinpoints that wink in and out. Keep exactly this hair colour; only the hairstyle is yours.\n\nExposure (fixed): bold — her outfit shows skin by design (a deep neckline,