em); intimate areas covered.\n\nFace proportions: a short midface and a soft, gently rounded jawline with a small soft chin; any crown or headpiece sits above her hairline. Her eyes keep the shape and size described above.\n\nComposition: vertical 2:3 full-body framing with modest headroom and clear space below the boots — the whole figure from the top of her head or headpiece to both feet stays inside the frame, occupying about four-fifths of the image height, with the same camera distance in every world; her hands stay inside the frame. Camera level with her face with natural portrait perspective; her head level, chin neither raised nor tucked — no upward perspective on her face, no wide-angle distortion, no low angle, no close crop.\n\nIf you have already drawn a free design of her in this session, make this one clearly different — another face and hairstyle (the same hair colour), another costume shape with another signature idea, another pose and setting.\n\nDetailed design for this image: Choose silhouette 2: cropped gunmetal-grey flight jacket with a long cold-grey-blue scarf, crossing leather harness straps, small brass goggles resting above her hairline; fitted short opaque pilot shorts and knee boots, open deep neckline with opaque intimate coverage and bare midriff and thighs. Signature construction: scarf ends divide into a descending sequence of narrower separated strips, and the jacket's cuff clasps form diminishing nested rings, echoing radioactive half-life. Faint violet seams and sparse pinpoint white studs. Adult woman with honey-beige skin, soft round-oval face, bright smoky grey eyes, tapered brows, small upturned nose, full soft lips, short midface and small round chin; playful determined smile. Metallic jet-black hair with faint violet sheen and tiny white pinpoints, long loose waves and side-swept bangs. Full front three-quarter stance, both empty human hands relaxed at her sides, fingers visible. On a sunlit outer laboratory terrace over the bay, a round cyclotron hall and glass vacuum apparatus behind her, small steam pipes integrated into the terrace; clear blue daylight. No weapon. One figure only, natural hands with five fingers; no text or numbers except her element's own chemical symbol (At) and atomic number (85) — and those only as part of the scene: engraved, embroidered or glowing on her costume, a banner, a sign or a machine, never as a floating label, corner badge, periodic-table tile, caption or overlay on the picture; no logo or watermark.",
