d blunt airy fringe. Stand facing the viewer beside a large brass-rimmed vacuum window showing a bismuth target, both empty hands clearly visible, one held slightly away from the coat's seam and the other relaxed. Bright daylight through the domed laboratory skylight, bay visible through a side window, analog gauges without readable markings. No weapon. One figure only, natural hands with five fingers; no text or numbers except her element's own chemical symbol (At) and atomic number (85) — and those only as part of the scene: engraved, embroidered or glowing on her costume, a banner, a sign or a machine, never as a floating label, corner badge, periodic-table tile, caption or overlay on the picture; no logo or watermark.",
